    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27521" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">măcŭlātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		maculo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a spotting; a spot, stain</i> (post-class.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cutem maculationibus convariare,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. Mag. p. 306, 14</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: aliquā infamiae maculatione
			pollutus, <i>stain</i>, Firm. Math. 3, 15, 3.</div>
